            "text": "$0.23 \\times 80$",
            "correct": true
          },
          {
            "id": "divide",
            "text": "$80 \\div 23$",
            "why": "You divided by the percentage. That finds one twenty-third, about 4.3%."
          },
          {
            "id": "tens",
            "text": "$23 \\times 8$",
            "why": "You took 23 lots of 10%, which is 230%. The unit should be 1%, worth 80p."
          },
          {
            "id": "inverse",
            "text": "$80 \\div 0.23$",
            "why": "You divided by the decimal. That gives more than £80, but 23% must be less than the whole."
          }
        ]
      },
      "hints": [
        {
          "rung": "nudge",
          "text": "23% is 23 hundredths."
        },
        {
          "rung": "step",
          "text": "$\\tfrac{23}{100} \\times 80 = 0.23 \\times 80 = 18.4$, so £18.40."
        }
      ],
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$0.23 \\times 80 = 18.4$, so £18.40.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Turn the percentage into hundredths, then multiply."
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "23% is 23 lots of 1%, and 1% of £80 is 80p. So 23% is $0.23 \\times 80 = £18.40$. One multiplication replaces the whole build."
      }
    },
